   "body": "Fixed on a fork branch: `fix/3828-opencode-bin-path` (head `127fee62`, on upstream `6eb510f7`) — OpenCode's own installer's opencode is the one found.\n\n**Root cause.** `internal/proc/path_other.go`'s known user-bin list (`.local/bin`, `.bun/bin`, …) and its Windows twin in `path_windows.go` had no `.opencode/bin`, so `FindTool(\"opencode\")` only found the stale one in `/opt/homebrew/bin` — and the issue's version read stayed 1.17.18.\n\n**Change.** `.opencode/bin` added to both lists, before `SystemDirs`, so the user's own install wins; `cliBin`'s ordering is untouched. The issue's second half (OpenCode 2's config paths) is not covered — that needs its own investigation and is out of this patch's scope.\n\n**Verified.** Red: `go test -tags nogui ./internal/proc/ -run TestFind` → `FindTool(\"opencode\")` returned the homebrew path (or nothing), not `<testhome>/.opencode/bin/opencode`\nGreen: `same command → `ok`; the package's other tests green` → `ok github.com/yetone/magpie/internal/proc`\n\nNot verified: a real OpenCode 2 install (no box with it here); the path is the installer's documented one. If the reporter's case is a shell whose PATH has homebrew first, `cliBin` would need one more line — say so and I'll add it.\n\nFull `go test -tags nogui ./...` over round 27's branches: 70 packages ok, 5 red (edit `TestWriteAtomicReadOnlyHardLink`, gateway's five, plugin `TestPluginSOCKSProxy`, provider's synctest fatal in `TestUnreadLoginsWriteErrorsKeepCredentials`, testenv `TestProgram`) — every one of them reproduces identically at base `6eb510f7` in this environment (umask 0027), so none is from this change.\n\nBranch: https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/3828-opencode-bin-path — no PR opened, this repo takes no external PRs; say the word if you'd rather have the patch inline here.",
