     "body": "Found while checking chenxiang0010's Discord question (#general 1565169112660058164); recorded in eee8ea027 (docs/subsystems/agent-wiring.md).\n\nmagpie writes OpenCode's `provider.magpie`, which both OpenCode 1.19.5 and 2.2.0 read (verified on mote, sandbox HOME, fake gateway). OpenCode 2's own \"Migrate from V1\" guide offers to convert a config to native `providers`. After that:\n- magpie treats OpenCode as unwired (it looks for `provider.magpie` only);\n- a later model-list update magpie writes to `provider.magpie` is ignored, since a native `providers` entry with the same id wins (packages/core/src/config/normalize.ts, migrateProviders, at v2.2.0);\n- OpenCode 1 loses magpie if it reads that file.\n\nNot hit by a reporter yet. Fix: read `providers.magpie` as wired, and update whichever entry exists (in its own shape: package/settings.baseURL/settings.apiKey), never writing both.",
